  "notes": "PRISM Repurposing Secondary, held-out-drug split with structural de-duplication (DRUG_IDs whose Morgan-ECFP4/InChIKey-connectivity groups straddle a split boundary are dropped from train: 9,065 train rows / 21 DRUG_IDs removed, train drugs 1040 -> 1019). State is the direct HVG-2000 identity projection (no PCA rotation, no train-response-derived cell statistics), so state_dim = 2000 rather than the 2003 used by the other bundles. Retrained 2026-09-01 with chemical-pathway dropout (chem_dropout=0.6: the 128-d chemical latent is zeroed on 60% of training rows with inverted-dropout scaling, active only under model.train() -- inference and state_dict layout are unchanged), seed 7, cuda:7, strict_repro deterministic runtime. Against a chem_dropout=0.0 control trained by the same script on byte-identical prepared data (same seed, same prepare_cache_key 7b358baf9d86fe6ff78afc1f, same HVG genes_sha256 be6aacbb2d545441106ad106de40e543562d4cbb5908b8bc9f50c7baaf2d8b28, identical split_audit), test within-drug PCC rises 0.2312 -> 0.2804 and within-drug Spearman 0.2352 -> 0.2761 (n=136,167 rows / 298 held-out drugs); the model-selection objective (val within-drug PCC) moves the same way, 0.2259 -> 0.2699. Retraining noise floor on this benchmark is ~0.015 within-drug PCC. Single seed per arm."
